\viewkind4\pard\cf1\fs32\b Read ping and traceroute results\b0\fs22\par\par
\pard\sa120 Ping measures whether a target answers an ICMP echo request and how long the reply takes. A timeout means no reply arrived within the limit; it does not by itself prove that the device is offline.\par
\pard\sa180\sb120\b\fs28 Example: a short observation\b0\fs22\par
\pard\li240\ri240\sa120\f1 Requests = 100\par
Replies = 98\par
Observed reply loss = 2%\par
Average latency = average of successful replies\f0\par
\pard\sa120 Traceroute asks routers along a path to respond. Some routers limit these responses while forwarding traffic normally. Compare intermediate-hop results with the destination before drawing conclusions.\par
\pard\sa120 For the proposed jitter display, we will document the exact formula and how missing samples are handled.\par
